                </td>
                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">The course <strong>Modern Separation Techniques</strong>&nbsp;have evolved alongside advancements in high-tech innovations and novel polymer materials, emerging as more optimized and advanced methods for separation. These techniques are widely applied in fields such as healthcare, life sciences, environmental science, and food technology.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">As a specialized elective course for graduate students in&nbsp;Pharmacy, Medicinal Chemistry (including Natural Medicinal Chemistry), and Pharmacognosy, this course will introduce the latest developments in separation technology, focusing on the principles and applications of several widely used modern separation techniques closely related to drug research and development.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">The course aims to familiarize students with cutting-edge advancements in separation science, broaden their professional knowledge, and cultivate their ability to effectively separate and purify compounds in scientific research. Ultimately, it seeks to enhance students' expertise and research competence.</span></p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="height:19.9000pt;">
                <td width=777 valign=center colspan=14 style="width:466.7000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
